# Tenant Isolation

- Tenant identity comes from authenticated context (JWT/middleware), not from client-chosen ids for authorization.
- Operational data lives under `data/tenants/{id}/` in server mode — do not write tenant ops to global `data/` root.
- Campaign workers must retain tenant binding for their lifetime (ADR 001).
- Clear/request-scoped ContextVar must not leak across tenants; workers use snapshots/registry.
- See `docs/adr/001-tenant-worker-isolation.md` and skill `tenant-isolation-max`.
- Cross-tenant regression tests are required for isolation-sensitive changes.
